rw,intro:"Every year to the bridge age is bought today — the first years in cash, every later year as one index-linked gilt maturing before the April it pays for. What is left is the engine: one world-equity fund you do not touch until the bridge ends. From then the State Pension arrives and the engine pays the rest of the schedule by a standing monthly withdrawal. Nothing is re-bought, nothing triggers, nothing ratchets — and the engine can run out, late. That is the honest trade: certainty for the expensive early years, market risk moved to the far end.",machine:(t,e)=>(window._beAge=t.signature.bridgeAge,{fn:J5,d:{years:t.signature.amountsByAge,startAge:e.startAge,B:t.signature.B,bridgeAge:t.signature.bridgeAge,cashYears:t.signature.cashYears,engineCone:t.signature.engineCone,wealthCone:t.cones.wealth,restCostFull:t.signature.restCostFull,failAgeP10:t.signature.failAgeP10,ruinMc:t.ruin.mc,engineE0:t.signature.engineE0,bridgeCost:t.signature.bridgeCost,pot:t.signature.pot}}),dials:(t,e)=>Gt("Bridge to age","bridgeAge",'type="number" min="56" max="90"',t.bridgeAge||window._beAge||67)+Gt("Years in cash first","cashYears",'type="number" min="0" max="10"',t.cashYears??3),verdict:(t,e)=>{const n=t.signature;return"<strong>Bridge to "+n.bridgeAge+": "+D(Math.round(n.bridgeCost))+" ("+Math.round(n.shareOfPot*100)+"% of the pot). Engine today: "+D(Math.round(n.engineE0))+".</strong> At "+n.bridgeAge+" the engine is worth a median "+D(Math.round(n.engineAtB.p50))+" (1-in-10 bad "+D(Math.round(n.engineAtB.p10))+", 1-in-10 good "+D(Math.round(n.engineAtB.p90))+")"+(n.restCostFull?"; buying the remaining years by contract would cost "+D(Math.round(n.restCostFull))+" that day":"")+". Drawing the rest from the engine, the money ran out before the horizon in <strong>"+t.ruin.mc.toFixed(0)+"%</strong> of futures and "+t.ruin.hist.toFixed(0)+"% of real histories"+(n.failAgeMedian?" — typically by "+Math.round(n.failAgeMedian):"")+". Nothing can go wrong before "+n.bridgeAge+"."},d